== Gemini's second pass on #711, 2026-11-06: four points, all taken
1. Writers beside the executor: REAL. kvQuiesce stopped the executor only for a write that gives a block past its end back, but the batched prefill, the three layer-major prefills and UploadKV run beside the executor, not on it: after pipelined ForwardNoLogits a prefill whose end reaches the last mapped block (a copy on write into a shared block 0, from 10 to 70 after 64 to 69) or an upload changed the table or K/V a forward still in flight reads. Now they stop the executor outright; the decode entries keep the rewind check (their own forwards in flight read only rows and entries below them, and never write a shared block). Red first, TestKVPages_prefillAndUploadStopTheExecutor: neither the prefill nor the upload stopped it.
2. The batched step: REAL, both halves. It mapped rows in their order and kept what earlier rows had mapped when a later one failed or a reclaim aborted it, so a slot answered reuse for a row never written (slot 2 held a block and answered 1 after G3d's aborted step), and a borrower row ahead of a guaranteed one took the last free block and was then stopped by the guaranteed row's reclaim, which running the rows alone would not have done. Now kvMapStep maps the rows within their slot's share first, then the borrowers; a refusal or an abort rolls every slot back to the sequence it had before its first row (trimming what it took), and recurrent state is zeroed only once every row has mapped. A release or reclaim the step caused stands, as it would alone. Red first: TestKVPages_stepMapsGuaranteedRowsFirst (308 blocks against 311 and the borrower answering 0 for its 10,240 rows) and G3d's step (3) (slot 2 holding 1 block, answering 1).
3. TestKV2_copyKVExact's comment: TRUE. Its "a shorter one leaves the rows above as they were" read a range that was empty in every case it had. The comment now says what holds, dst has no row past the range, and the test reads that in every case.
4. The raise's memory: TAKEN, as two changes. (a) decoder.Model.MetalKVCap is now the raise's one rule (kvRaise calls it), and MetalKVBytes, the Metal fit (on the load's KV, once) and the build guard (for the slots asked) price every slot's block table at the raised cap (MetalKVTableRaiseBytes): 1,248 B at 2 slots of 9,984 and 3,072 B at 4 slots of 4,096 on the MC3 fixture, the bytes the plan had missed. (b) An int8 cache no longer raises: its prefill dequantizes the whole context into an f16 scratch sized to the cap, which the fit does not price (pricing it in ResidentKVBytes would put a pass's scratch on the kv line, which TestMemGate_metal holds exact to what is resident). Red first, TestMetalKVBytes_pricesTheRaisedTables: 1,248 B and 3,072 B short, and the int8 load raised. The parity manifest stays fresh (43 of 43 enforced): neither decoder file is a forward dependency. ResidentKVBytes (one slot) is unchanged, so no census row moves.
5. G3c re-runs on the final tree, and G2's cells whose code changed (MC3 through the step, TTFT through the prefill) re-read on it; the decode cells read on 2ffc982e (1.5B and gemma3-1b, 09:19 to 09:32 PST) ran the decode path this round does not touch.
Plants, 8 of 8 red (09:53 to 09:55): the batched prefill not stopping the executor; UploadKV not stopping it; the step not rolling back; the step mapping in arrival order (its first form did not build: re-planted so it does, red); a copy keeping dst rows past the range; the raised tables unpriced; an int8 cache raising; the fit leaving the raised tables out (red in decoder's TestMetalFitCtx_slotsTradeContext). Not planted: the build guard's addend, which only makes admission a few KB more conservative.
The KV, pricing and memory-gate tests after the fixes: 109 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped (GOINFER_METAL_MC3); decoder's Metal fit and plan tests 11 of 11; fitcmd ok.

The pricing moves MM1's decision census (testdata/mm1_census.json.gz), so it is re-recorded for both host classes: arm64 on this Mac and amd64 under Rosetta, which reproduces CI's class (main 4db6cd19's amd64 census matches the committed golden under Rosetta, 29,637 groups). On both, main's and the branch's full dumps differ in 7,244 lines of 399,765, and with the byte figures taken out they are identical: no decision moved, no context, slot count or reason. Each changed line's kv figure rises by what the raised tables add, 256 B to 6,144 B, and the free edges where a decision turns move with it. TestMetalFit_agreesWithSlotPricing now holds the fit and the build guard to the same bytes with the guard's addend in them.
