== Gemini's fourth pass on #711, 2026-11-07: three points taken, red first; the nit not taken
1. The chain's look-ahead after stopChain: REAL. The look-ahead the chain queues past the last token taken left the slot one row past its caller's sequence, and a block when it crossed an edge. The chain now records where its caller's sequence ends (chainEnd: after the newest forward whose token it returned) and stopChain ends the slot there (kvEndAt). Through the decoder, TestKVPages_chainEndsAtTheLastTokenTaken: a 62-token prompt and 2 tokens left 65 rows in 2 blocks against the decoder's 64 in 1. (The decoder's sequence is the prompt and every emitted token, each fed: residentCommitIDs; the first form of the test, a 63-token prompt, read 66 rows and wanted 64, and the fixed code's 65 showed the want was one short.) TestKVPages_chainReopensAfterAFailedTake now reads the block during the look-ahead and its release after.
2. CopyKV read state before stopExec: REAL once 1 is fixed, since the stop then changes src's sequence. It stops first. TestKVPages_copyJudgesTheSourceAfterTheChainStops: with the look-ahead's block mapped, a copy of [0, 128) was accepted and one table entry named the null block (red with 1 fixed and the old order); it now declines.
3. The clamp in UploadKV and kvWriteMust: TAKEN as a refusal outside a pass. Metal now has decoder.ResidentKVUploadPass, as CUDA does, which the decoder's upload (residentUploadPrefill) already calls: between BeginKVUpload and EndKVUpload the uploads are one write of the bound slot from position 0; the first layer maps the slot through its end, every layer that owns K/V must land once and at that end, a full-attention layer starts at 0, and a windowed layer may start late only where its rows cover its window (the decoder's reuse floor keeps a prefix off the rows below). Outside a pass an upload past the sequence is refused, and so is setPos's own write, as any unmapped write is; a test that picks the depth maps first (setPosAheadForTest, in the five test hooks and seven kernel-test sites that set a depth). Red first: TestKVPages_writePastTheSequenceRefused (an upload at 70 into an empty slot was accepted and answered 71), TestKVPages_uploadPass (no pass on Metal), TestKVPages_setPosPastTheSequencePanics (setPos(200) on an empty slot mapped 4 blocks). TestUploadKV_slidingLayerStartsLate holds gemma2-tiny (window 4, rings wrapped at 20 positions) through the decoder's own pass against a sequential resident prefill, at the cross-path bar 0.999 of the int8 KV variant (it reads 0.9997 on the old code too: CPU against device K/V, not the upload).
5. Decode's two kvWrite calls a token: NOT TAKEN. setPos's write is the guard for paths that reach it without an entry point; dropping either is not free.
Plants, 8 of 8 red: stopChain not ending the slot; CopyKV stopping after it reads; an upload outside a pass mapping from the sequence's end; a full-attention layer starting late in a pass; EndKVUpload not checking every layer; a layer ending elsewhere; a layer uploading twice; setPos mapping from the sequence's end.
The Metal package whole (-tags goinfer_testhooks, eb90144b): 457 passed, 220 skipped, 0 failed.
The decode path changed (the chain's stop, setPos's write), so the 7B night job is re-pinned to eb90144b.

